# ----------------------------------------------------------- api-diff: comparing

[break] api-judges-a-change-on-what-is-shown
rule: A change is judged on the signature without the names of arguments, not on how it is shown.
file: xtask/src/api_diff/diff.rs
in: compare
find: old.kind != entry.kind || old.identity != entry.identity
replace: old.kind != entry.kind || old.shown != entry.shown
caught-by:
    api_diff::diff::tests::a_change_is_judged_on_the_identity_and_not_on_what_is_shown

[break] api-ignores-a-change-of-kind
rule: An item that became another kind is changed even if its signature reads the same.
file: xtask/src/api_diff/diff.rs
in: compare
find: old.kind != entry.kind ||
replace: false ||
caught-by:
    api_diff::diff::tests::an_item_that_became_another_kind_is_changed_even_with_one_signature

[break] api-lists-the-impls-of-an-added-type
rule: The impls of a type added in the same change come with the type and are not listed beside it.
file: xtask/src/api_diff/diff.rs
in: compare
find: .is_some_and(|owner| added_paths.contains(owner));
replace: .is_some_and(|owner| owner.is_empty());
caught-by:
    api_diff::diff::tests::the_impls_of_a_type_added_or_removed_with_it_are_not_listed_beside_it

[break] api-lists-the-impls-of-a-removed-type
rule: The impls of a type removed in the same change go with the type and are not listed beside it.
file: xtask/src/api_diff/diff.rs
in: compare
find: .is_some_and(|owner| removed_paths.contains(owner));
replace: .is_some_and(|owner| owner.is_empty());
caught-by:
    api_diff::diff::tests::the_impls_of_a_type_added_or_removed_with_it_are_not_listed_beside_it

[break] api-lists-in-the-wrong-order
rule: The report is in the order of the paths, the same every run.
file: xtask/src/api_diff/diff.rs
in: compare
find: deltas.sort_by(|a, b| a.key.cmp(&b.key));
replace: deltas.sort_by(|a, b| b.key.cmp(&a.key));
caught-by:
    api_diff::diff::tests::items_added_removed_and_changed_come_out_in_the_order_of_their_paths

[break] api-breaks-a-markdown-table-on-a-bar
rule: A `|` in a signature is escaped in a Markdown table, or it ends the cell.
file: xtask/src/api_diff/diff.rs
in: code
find: text.replace('|', "\\|")
replace: text.to_owned()
caught-by:
    api_diff::diff::tests::the_report_as_markdown_is_a_table_for_each_crate_with_changes

[break] api-names-the-crates-that-changed-as-unchanged
rule: The crates with no difference are named on one line, and those with differences are not.
file: xtask/src/api_diff/diff.rs
in: unchanged
find: .filter(|krate| krate.deltas.is_empty())
replace: .filter(|krate| !krate.deltas.is_empty())
caught-by:
    api_diff::diff::tests::the_report_as_text_has_a_line_for_an_addition_and_three_for_a_change
    api_diff::diff::tests::the_report_as_markdown_is_a_table_for_each_crate_with_changes

