[break] api-takes-markdown-for-text
rule: `--format markdown` is read, and anything else but `text` is refused.
file: xtask/src/api_diff.rs
in: parse
find: "markdown" | "md" => Format::Markdown,
replace: "markdown" | "md" => Format::Text,
caught-by:
    api_diff::tests::a_request_is_read

[break] api-documents-with-the-stable-compiler-alone
rule: rustdoc's JSON needs unstable options, which the pinned stable toolchain takes with RUSTC_BOOTSTRAP=1.
file: xtask/src/api_diff.rs
in: document
find: .env("RUSTC_BOOTSTRAP", "1")
replace: .env("RUSTC_BOOTSTRAP", "0")
expect: survives

[break] api-asks-rustdoc-for-html
rule: The flags ask rustdoc for JSON. Only the ignored `sys_the_real` test of `api_diff` runs rustdoc, and `mutate` runs no ignored test, so it is not caught here; `cargo xtask test -p xtask --run-ignored only sys_the_real` is what catches it.
file: xtask/src/api_diff.rs
find: const RUSTDOCFLAGS: &str = "-Z unstable-options --output-format json";
replace: const RUSTDOCFLAGS: &str = "-Z unstable-options";
expect: survives

